      },
      "message": "Tighten vector construction guards and native regressions\n\nAvoid redundant vector scans, preserve disabled-construction constant and splat coverage, test the ordinary C path with inlining disabled, and distinguish the proven output-pointer spill from prohibited construction memory traffic.\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>\nSigned-off-by: David Gonzalez Martin <davidgmbb@gmail.com>",
